1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,085
LANTERN. Lightweight navigation.

2
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:08,786
A compact encoder and shared decoder produce candidate curves and scores.

3
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:13,476
One depth frame and motion state yield twenty-four candidate trajectories.

4
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:20,367
Directional geometry anchors queries. Cross-attention reads image features with an angular prior.

5
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:25,264
The learned readout adapts to geometry; the fixed-grid panel is schematic.

6
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:30,562
Quintic Bezier curves match the initial position, velocity, and acceleration.

7
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:36,153
Directional anchors preserve coverage; bounded residuals adapt the curves to obstacles.

8
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:45,114
Near the goal, six queries become goal-relative. Their control points
contract toward the goal, supporting deceleration and stopping.

9
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:51,267
One differentiable cost combines smoothness, obstacle avoidance, progress, and settling.

10
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:57,354
Low-cost candidates receive more training weight. Their costs also supervise scores.

11
00:00:57,820 --> 00:01:02,724
Rebuilding from the handoff state preserves reference continuity when tracking remains close.

12
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:09,472
LANTERN succeeds in one hundred ninety-six of two hundred fixed-seed trials.

13
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:14,296
Network forward: one point one nine milliseconds.

14
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:22,131
Separate five-meter-per-second examples show dense and sparse forests. All flight recordings play at normal speed.

15
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:30,763
The same planners are compared in box clutter and wall corridors, with their recorded speed shown below.

16
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:39,648
Selected eight-meter-per-second runs show dense pillars, boxes, and walls.

17
00:01:55,220 --> 00:02:08,218
This independent example compares three planners. LANTERN settles near the goal. With no
goal queries, the vehicle collides; YOPO keeps moving. Ended panels hold their recorded states.

18
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:14,968
Fifty trials: fifty strict stops for LANTERN, zero for both comparisons.

19
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:22,749
Finally, indoor and outdoor flights demonstrate the deployed
planner. The speed gauges follow recorded motion estimates.

20
00:02:52,187 --> 00:03:01,807
Candidate trajectories, the executed path, and the onboard view remain synchronized.
The dial displays the original velocity estimate without temporal smoothing.

21
00:03:14,287 --> 00:03:15,100
LANTERN.
